Two bodies each declaring one name, for all three type kinds.

A `struct`, `enum` or `unit` written in a body is scoped to that body, so the
three declarations named `Local` here are three distinct types and the checker
is right to let all three through. What the checker cannot fix is where they
land: a body-local declaration still joins `ir.Package.Structs`, which is what
every backend emits type declarations from, and no host has a body to scope one
to. Before `passHoistBodyTypes` this program emitted `type Local struct` twice
in one Go file, `type Tick float64` twice beside it, and `sngl generate` exited
0 on output that does not compile. An interim checker error stood in for the
pass and is what it removes.

The first claimant keeps its spelling and the rest are renamed after the body
they were written in, so read below: `Local` is `first`'s, `Local__second` is
`second`'s, and `Local__pick` belongs to a function body rather than a
component's. `Phase`/`Phase__second` and `Tick`/`Tick__second` say the same for
the other two kinds.

`doubled` is a method on the renamed-past declaration, which is the one
reference site that does not ride on the declaration pointer: `ir.Func.Receiver`
is the receiver type's name written out as a string.

`rows` is a `list[Local]` in the body whose `Local` moved, so the element of a
generic type is covered too -- Go spells it `[]Local__second`.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `(?s)type Tick float64.*type Tick float64` -- one Go file, one declaration of each name: two bodies declaring `unit Tick` is the unit half of what this pass fixes
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `type Local struct \{\n\tBField string` -- second's fields must never arrive under first's name
deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `(?s)data class Local\(.*data class Local\(` -- Kotlin declares its types too, so the same collision lands there
deny out/none/html/index.html `(?s)function Local\(.*function Local\(` -- JavaScript declares no types but does emit a constructor per struct, so the second one silently replaced the first

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
    none {
        html
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

func pick(n int) int {
    struct Local {
        c int
    }

    var v Local = Local{c=n}
    return v.c
}

component first node {
    struct Local {
        a int

        func doubled() => this.a * 2
    }
    enum Phase {
        start
        done
    }
    unit Tick {
        beat
    }

    var here = Local{a=1}
    var p = Phase.done
    var elapsed Tick = 3beat

    text(value="{here.doubled()}")
    text(value="{int(elapsed)}")
    if p == Phase.done {
        text(value="first done")
    }
}

component second node {
    struct Local {
        bField string

        // Recursive, so the inliner leaves it standing and the emitted method
        // carries the renamed receiver.
        func shout(n int) string {
            if n <= 0 {
                return this.bField
            }
            return this.shout(n - 1)
        }
    }
    enum Phase {
        ready
    }
    unit Tick {
        span
    }

    var here = Local{bField="two"}
    var rows list[Local] = []
    var p = Phase.ready
    var elapsed Tick = 5span

    text(value="{here.shout(2)}")
    text(value="{rows.length()}")
    text(value="{int(elapsed)}")
    if p == Phase.ready {
        text(value="second ready")
    }
}

component main node {
    var seed = 2

    first()
    second()
    text(value="{pick(seed)}")
}

window {
    main
}
